<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $210.9 mln Sept 12.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $210.9 mln Sept 12.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $210.9 million deficit on Sept 12 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 12</p>
<p>Exports: $212.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $255.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $125.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $292.9 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $210.9 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.888 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.396 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.171 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.901 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $238 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroom 55-11-2324411</p>
